#CPU 
1. it's the called the brain of the computer sys, containing cores and treads.
2. cores are (like cells in a brain) . each are assigned an instruction to be preformed .
{imp: core speed > number of cores}
3. earlier cpu had 1 core which performed 1 task. it juggled so fast giving an illusion of multi-tasking
4. cpu threads are virtual extension of physical core.[like adding 2 more hands to a person]
5.performance doesn't double just coz we have more threads. threads are good in parallel execution.

#RAM 
1. they are the primary storage unit. the stored data is erased when the sys is off.
2. however they help in fast access of info whenever the cpu needs. large amt of data can't be stored.

#SSD/HDD
